{
  "slug": "cxpak",
  "name": "Cxpak",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Token-budgeted codebase context for Claude Code. One call to auto_context gives Claude the optimal context for any task — automatically selecting, ranking, noise-filtering, and packing the most relevant code from your entire codebase. 11 MCP tools including symbol tracing, blast radius analysis, API surface extraction, and semantic search. Supports 42 programming languages via tree-sitter.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **3 skills**, **4 commands** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (3): `codebase-context` (Use when the user asks about codebase structure, architecture, what a project does, how components relate, or needs…), `diff-context` (Use when the user asks to review changes, understand what changed, prepare a PR description, or needs context…), `setup` (Set up the cxpak MCP server for the current project)\n- **Commands** (4): `clean` (Clear the cxpak cache and output files), `diff` (Run cxpak diff to show changes with dependency context within a token budget), `overview` (Run cxpak overview to get structured codebase context within a token budget), `trace` (Run cxpak trace to find a symbol and pack relevant code paths within a token budget)\n- **MCP servers** (1): `cxpak`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install cxpak@claude-community` from `Barnett-Studios/cxpak` (`plugin`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 3,
    "command": 4,
    "mcp": 1
  },
